docs-title = Documentation
docs-intro = Everything about how Mitsuzo works: the cryptography, the API, and running your own server.
docs-security-title = Security Model
docs-security-desc = The complete key hierarchy behind envelope encryption — the short version of what the server actually sees.
docs-security-item1 = Content key (CEK): random 32 bytes per paste, encrypts every data chunk
docs-security-item2 = Key-encryption key: KEK = HKDF-SHA256(Argon2id(password, salt), "mitsuzo-encryption-key")
docs-security-item3 = CEK is wrapped with ChaCha20-Poly1305(KEK, wrap_nonce) into a 48-byte wrapped key, stored server-side
docs-security-item4 = Password change: unwrap CEK with the old KEK, re-wrap with the new KEK — the ciphertext is never touched
docs-security-item5 = Validation: HMAC-SHA256(HKDF(master, "mitsuzo-validation-key"), salt), compared in constant time by the server
docs-security-item6 = Burn receipt: HKDF-SHA256(CEK, "mitsuzo-burn-receipt") — derived from the content key, so it stays valid across password changes
docs-security-item7 = Legacy pastes created before envelope encryption decrypt via the old direct derived-key path
docs-api-title = API Reference
docs-api-desc = All bodies are bitcode-encoded binary. Content endpoints require X-Password-Hash: base64(HMAC-SHA256(validation_key, salt)); failed attempts decrement the paste try count.
docs-api-init = Initialize a paste — body: CreatePasteHeader, response contains the new paste id
docs-api-chunk-put = Upload one 16 MB upload-chunk of ciphertext
docs-api-chunks = Received upload-chunk count (resumable uploads)
docs-api-complete = Finalize a paste upload
docs-api-salt = Bootstrap only: the Argon2id salt (required to derive the password hash) — no paste metadata is exposed here
docs-api-data = Download ciphertext — X-Password-Hash required, Range supported; response is [metadata frame (nonce, file info, wrapped key, try count)] + ciphertext
docs-api-get = Download framed GetPasteHeader + ciphertext
docs-api-password = Change password — body: new salt/wrapped key/hash, X-Password-Hash carries the old hash
docs-api-burn = Burn-after-read receipt — deletes the paste on match
docs-api-stats = Anonymous usage counters
docs-api-account = Register an account — body: RegisterAccountRequest (kid, pubkey, name); server recomputes kid from pubkey and rejects mismatches
docs-api-account-get = Public profile (pubkey + name) for a kid (full 32-byte hash or 20-byte prefix)
docs-api-account-challenge = Single-use login challenge sealed to the account public key — solve it and return the response nonce
docs-api-account-name = Change the display name — body: ChangeNameRequest(name, challenge_response)
